  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 151 AM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nMonsoon moisture remains entrenched. Another shortwave will \npass through the area today. With the better support across the \ncentral mountains, they should see the best coverage today. \nIsolated to scattered coverage is expected elsewhere. Once \nagain, the potential for heavy rain exists because of the \nmonsoon. The threat appears less today across the Big Rock area,\nbut not zero. Better chances across the Wapiti once again where\nthe Flash Flood Watch remains in effect. \n\nThe monsoon moisture will hang around until midweek. Although the \nsystems between Sunday and then look relatively weak. Still heating \nof the day will be sufficient to trigger isolated thunderstorms as \nthe high res models are now suggesting. Models show the ridge \namplifying over the Intermountain West later in the week. Although \nits uncertain if we get another monsoon push associated with it. The \nridge axis may be a little too directly overhead to allow for much \nthunderstorm development. \n\nTemps will remain below normal through midweek. But should return to \nnear normal by late week.",
